# gstack /browse + investing auth

`/browse` uses Playwright Chromium (`~/.gstack/chromium-profile`), not daily Chrome.

Cursor often sets `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` to an empty sandbox cache. Before any `$B` call:

```bash
B="$HOME/.claude/skills/gstack/browse/dist/browse"
unset PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH
export PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH="$HOME/Library/Caches/ms-playwright"
export GSTACK_CHROMIUM_PATH="$HOME/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium-1208/chrome-mac-arm64/Google Chrome for Testing.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome for Testing"
```

If daemon already `Mode: headed`, pass `--headed` on every command (or config mismatch).

Before opening `lavega.dev` / `www.lavega.dev` /investing:

```bash
$B state load lavega-investing
```

If load fails or page is sign-in:

```bash
$B --headed goto https://www.lavega.dev/investing
$B --headed focus
```

Stop. User logs in in the visible window. After they say done:

```bash
$B state save lavega-investing
```

Do not dump cookie values into chat. Confirm with URL + that the page is not `/sign-in`.
